### Key decisions explained

| Decision | Reason |
|---|---|
| `InfoCard` wrapper | Backstage's standard card container; provides consistent title bar, padding, and theming out of the box. |
| `makeStyles` with theme tokens | Backstage uses Material UI v4's `makeStyles`; using `theme.spacing` and `theme.palette` keeps the component theme-aware and avoids hardcoded values. |
| `renderInTestApp` in tests | Backstage components depend on app-level contexts (routing, themes). `renderInTestApp` wires those up correctly. |
| JSDoc `@public` tag | Backstage uses API Extractor; tagging the export tells it this symbol is part of the public API surface. |
| Named export (not default) | Backstage convention is named exports for all plugin components to make tree-shaking and re-exports predictable. |
| `aria-label` on `Avatar` | Accessibility — the avatar is purely visual, so a label associates it with the user's name for screen readers. |

